NAME
       lvdisplay - show the details of logical volumes

SYNOPSIS
       lvdisplay [-m] [-C] [VG | VG/LV]...

DESCRIPTION
       lvdisplay prints a block of details for each logical volume (or the
       ones named): LV Path, LV Name, VG Name, LV UUID, LV Status (available
       when active), LV Size, Current LE (its size in extents) and more.

       lvs prints the same information as a short table, one line per LV,
       which is easier for checking and for scripts (lvs --noheadings -o
       lv_size vg/lv).

OPTIONS
       -m, --maps
              Also show which physical volumes and extents the LV uses.

       -C, --columns
              Print a table, like lvs.

EXAMPLES
           lvdisplay vgdata/lvdata
           lvdisplay -m vgdata/lvdata

SEE ALSO
       lvs(8), vgdisplay(8), pvdisplay(8), lvcreate(8)
